{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 520,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine I offered you a deal. That sounds \nlike a mathematical error. I want you to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6600,
    "dDurationMs": 8480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "take a 20% pay cut. In exchange, I am going to \nincrease your total annual free time by 50%.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16840,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most people hear that 20% drop and their survival \ninstincts kick in. They think about the mortgage,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23200,
    "dDurationMs": 7240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the groceries, and that rising utility bill. But \nif you actually run the numbers, and I mean really  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30440,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dig into the tax code and the hidden costs of your \ncubicle, you will realize that your fifth day of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36560,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "work is probably the least profitable day of your \nentire week. For over a century, we have treated  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43720,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the 40hour work week like a law of physics. \nWe treat it like gravity or thermodynamics.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51480,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the 40-hour week was actually a compromise \ndesigned for factory workers in the 1920s.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58200,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was never meant for the modern knowledge \nworker. Today, we are going to look at the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63800,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "4-day work week not as a lifestyle trend, but \nas a hard-nosed financial optimization problem.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71680,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We are going to calculate exactly why giving up \n20% of your gross income might be the smartest  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77600,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "investment you ever make and how the government \nactually ends up subsidizing your 3-day weekend.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85480,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Before we dismantle your budget, \nwe need to agree on one thing.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90120,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Money is a renewable resource. You can \nearn more, save more, or invest better.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96880,
    "dDurationMs": 6760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But time is strictly finite. It is a depreciating \nasset that you can never buy back once it is gone.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104800,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you are watching this, you probably care \nabout the return on investment for your capital.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what about the return on investment for \nyour life? If you find this kind of deep dive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114720,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "financial analysis useful, the best ROI you can \nget right now is hitting that subscribe button.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121200,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It tells the algorithm that you value \nlong-term strategy over getquick rich schemes.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126880,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "My goal here is to help you build a financial life \nthat serves your time, not the other way around.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132960,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We are going to look at the 4-day work week \nthrough the lens of taxes, commuting, child care,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138480,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and human capital. This is not about being lazy. \nIt is about being mathematically efficient.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145320,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the end of this, you will know if you can \nafford to buy back your life or if you are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149840,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "currently paying too high a price for your fifth \nday in the office. Let us start with the biggest  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156400,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "myth in personal finance. The idea that gross \nsalary is a real number. It is not. It is a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163600,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vanity metric. The only number that matters for \nyour quality of life is your net takehome pay.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171880,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you think about a 20% pay cut, you are \nlikely envisioning 20% of your standard of living  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177400,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "disappearing. But that is not how progressive tax \nsystems work. In countries like the United States,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185080,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your income is taxed in brackets. Your \nfirst dollars are taxed at almost nothing,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191280,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and your last dollars are taxed at your highest \nmarginal rate. When you drop from a 5-day week  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197680,
    "dDurationMs": 7800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a 4-day week, you aren't losing the bottom 20% \nof your income. You are slicing off the top 20%.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206400,
    "dDurationMs": 7240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That top slice is what I call the high tax \nzone. For an individual earning $100,000,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213640,
    "dDurationMs": 7640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that top 20,000 is likely being hit by a \n22% federal rate plus FICA plus state taxes.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222360,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you remove that income, your total \ntax bill doesn't just drop, it collapses.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228360,
    "dDurationMs": 8160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In many cases, a 20% gross pay cut only results \nin a 14 or 15% drop in your actual spending power.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237480,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The government is essentially footing the \nbill for a portion of your new day off.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242800,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are trading your most heavily taxed hours \nfor 100% tax-free leisure time. I want to put  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250160,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some real numbers behind this because it is \neasy to nod along until you see the math.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256400,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's take a professional earning $80,000 a \nyear. After federal taxes, social security,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263200,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a typical state tax, their monthly \ntake-home pay might be around $5,000.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270520,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, if they take a 20% cut to $64,000, \ntheir gross pay drops by $16,000 a year,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279440,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but because they are now in a lower \noverall effective tax bracket,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283600,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their monthly take-home \nonly drops to about $4,200."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289680,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The difference in their pocket is $800, not \nthe $1,300 they expected from the gross math.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298680,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That $800 is the price of four \nextra days off every single month.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304680,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means they are paying $200 for \nevery extra Friday they stay home.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311080,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To some, $200 sounds like a lot. But when you \nfactor in that this person is gaining 52 extra  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318240,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "days a year, they are essentially buying back \nnearly two months of their life for a relatively  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324520,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "small adjustment in their net cash flow. This \nis the tax efficiency of the 4-day work week.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332440,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are giving up your least valuable \ndollars to reclaim your most valuable time.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338840,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you really want to be honest with yourself, \nyou need to calculate your real hourly wage.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345560,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most people take their salary and divide \nit by 2,000 hours. That is a mistake.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352720,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your job doesn't just cost you the 8 hours you \nare at your desk. It costs you the commute,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359360,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the time you spend prepping your clothes, and the \ntwo hours every evening you spend decompressing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365600,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because you are too exhausted to do anything else. \nIf you work 40 hours but spend 10 hours commuting  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373280,
    "dDurationMs": 9320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 5 hours recovering, your actual work rellated \ntime is 55 hours. When you shift to a 4-day week,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382600,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you don't just lose 8 hours of work. You gain back \n2 hours of commuting and an hour of recovery time.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390800,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your total time dedicated to the \nmachine drops from 55 hours to 44.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398000,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you divide your new slightly lower net \npay by these significantly lower total hours,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404840,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something fascinating happens. your \nreal hourly wage almost always goes up.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412400,
    "dDurationMs": 6345,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are literally making your time more valuable \nby working less of it. You are cutting the low  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418745,
    "dDurationMs": 5535,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "value fluff and focusing your energy on the \nfour days where you are actually productive.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425640,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From a purely economic standpoint, \nyou are moving from a high volume  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429800,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "low margin business model to a boutique \nhigh margin model for your own labor.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436360,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We need to address the psychological ratio of \nthe week. In a standard 5-day model, you have a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441960,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2.5:1 ratio of labor to leisure. You work 2 and \n1/2 days for every 1 day you get to yourself.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450280,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That ratio is barely enough for most people \nto maintain their sanity, let alone thrive.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456640,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you move to a 4-day week, \nthat ratio shifts to 1.3:1.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461920,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are nearly doubling the ratio of your \nfreedom. This is what I call the 50% dividend.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468920,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By cutting your work days by 20%. You have \nincreased your weekend by 50%. That extra day  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476280,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a massive structural change. It is the day you \ncan run errands when the stores aren't crowded.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483360,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is the day you can visit a doctor without \ntaking sick leave. It is the day you can finally  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489000,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "start that project you have been putting off for \n3 years. The financial value of that extra day  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495360,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn't just about what you don't spend. It \nis about the mental clarity it provides.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501240,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That clarity often leads to better financial \ndecisions in every other area of your life.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507280,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you are not exhausted, you don't make impulse \npurchases to numb the pain of a 60-hour grind.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514280,
    "dDurationMs": 8400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let us talk about the invisible tax on employment. \nWorking is expensive. Most people don't realize  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522680,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how much of their income is just reinvested \nback into the act of being an employee.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528800,
    "dDurationMs": 6760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Commuting is the most obvious offender. The \naverage American spends nearly $10,000 a year just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535560,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on transportation. When you eliminate one day of \ncommuting per week, you are not just saving gas.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are reducing the wear and tear on your \nvehicle, which slows down depreciation  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547400,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and pushes back the date you'll need to buy \na new car. You are reducing your oil changes,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553160,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your tire rotations, and your insurance \nrisk. If you use public transit,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558720,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you might be able to switch from a monthly pass \nto a per ride model that saves you hundreds.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565120,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the savings go deeper than the gas tank. Think \nabout your professional wardrobe. Dry cleaning  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571520,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bills and the cost of replacing work shoes and \nsuits are all tied to the frequency of use.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578360,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Reducing your office presence by 20% extends \nthe life of your professional assets by 20%.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585200,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over a decade, that is thousands of dollars \nthat stay in your brokerage account instead  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589680,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of going to the tailor. These are small leaks \nthat when plugged start to make that 20% pay cut  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596800,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "look more like a minor adjustment than \na catastrophe. When you are time poor,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602200,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you are forced to buy convenience. This is \na fundamental law of behavioral finance.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607920,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you get home at 7:00 p.m. after a 10-hour \nday and a brutal commute, you are not going  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613000,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to roast a chicken and prep a salad for \ntomorrow. You are going to order delivery.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618280,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are going to pay a $15 service fee \nand a $5 tip for a mediocre bowl of pasta.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 624400,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the convenience tax. A 5-day work week is \na factory for this kind of spending. You buy the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631200,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "expensive coffee because you need the caffeine \nhit to make it through the 3 p.m. meeting.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636440,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You buy the pre-cut vegetables because \nyou don't have 10 minutes to use a knife.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641280,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you gain that extra day, you are effectively \ninsourcing your life. You have the time to meal  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647000,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prep on your extra day off. You can shop at three \ndifferent grocery stores to get the best prices  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652680,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instead of just grabbing whatever is closest to \nthe office. I've seen people save $3 to $400 a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658560,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "month just by having the time to be intentional \nwith their food. If you save $4,000 a year on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "food and convenience, that is equivalent \nto earning nearly $6,000 in gross salary.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 671560,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Suddenly, the gap between your old salary and your \nnew 4-day salary is closing faster than you think.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678360,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your time is literally becoming your currency. \nIf you think this sounds like a perfect plan,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684600,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I need you to pause because there is a trap \nhere that could cost you hundreds of thousands  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690200,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of dollars if you aren't careful. We've talked \nabout the immediate savings and they are great,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696400,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but finance is a game of decades, \nnot days. If you take a 20% pay cut  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and simply adjust your lifestyle to match, you're \ngoing to walk straight into a retirement disaster.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708440,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most people contribute to their retirement \naccounts based on a percentage of their pay.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713520,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If your pay drops from 80,000 to 64,000 \nand you keep your contribution at 10%,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719640,
    "dDurationMs": 8720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you are saving $1,600 less per year. Over 30 \nyears, with a 7% return, that small gap balloons  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728360,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into a massive deficit. We are talking about \nnearly $200,000 of missing wealth. You cannot just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735880,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "work less and hope for the best. You have to be \neven more disciplined with the money you do have.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742440,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to take this path, you need to \nunderstand the concept of the compounding penalty.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 748080,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In a moment, I'm going to show you how \nto neutralize this risk. But first,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752640,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we need to look at the other hidden costs that \nyour HR department probably won't tell you about.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759000,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The retirement deficit isn't just about your \nown contributions. It is about the free money  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764120,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you are leaving on the table. Most employers offer \na matching contribution up to a certain percentage  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770280,
    "dDurationMs": 8160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of your salary. If your company matches 5% and \nyour salary drops by $16,000, you just lost an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778440,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "$800 annual bonus from your boss, that is money \nthat would have compounded tax-free for decades.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786480,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To combat this, you have to be willing to \nincrease your personal contribution percentage.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792080,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you were saving 10% on a 5-day salary, you \nmight need to save 13 or 14% on your 4-day salary  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799600,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to keep your absolute dollar contributions the \nsame. This is the part where most people fail.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 806440,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They want the free time, but they aren't willing \nto tighten the belt to protect their future self.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812880,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You also have to consider the \nsocial security implications.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817000,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the US, your benefits are based \non your 35 highest earning years.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822440,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you spend 15 years working 4 days a \nweek, your lifetime average will be lower  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828000,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and your monthly check in retirement will shrink. \nIt is a modest hit, but it is a permanent one.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835400,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are trading a portion of your elder self's \nsecurity for your current self's freedom.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841000,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That might be a trade you are willing to make, but \nyou must make it with your eyes wide open. There  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 846800,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a psychological cost to working 4 days that \ndoesn't show up on a spreadsheet. Proximity bias.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854400,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We like to think that corporate culture is a \nmeritocracy, but human nature says otherwise.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 860840,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Managers tend to favor the people they see \nmost often. If there is a high-profile project  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866320,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that needs a leader on a Friday morning \nand you are at the park with your dog,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870880,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you aren't getting that project. Over time, being \nthe 4-day person can slow your career trajectory.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879080,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You might miss out on a promotion \nthat would have come with a 15% raise.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 883960,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If your peers are moving up while you are staying \nlevel, the income gap between your current path  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 889320,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and your potential path grows exponentially \nevery year. This is the career opportunity cost.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 897160,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You have to decide if you are okay \nwith being on the slower track.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901320,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For some, the slower track is a blessing. \nIt means less stress and more boundaries.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 907640,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for someone with high earning ambitions, \na 4-day schedule can act as a glass ceiling.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 913680,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You have to be twice as productive in \nyour 32 hours as your peers are in 40  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 918560,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just to remain visible. You are essentially paying \nfor your Friday with your future career growth.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925760,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is 52 days a year worth a slower climb to \nthe seauite? For me, the answer is often yes.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 932600,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for you, it depends on what you value more, \nthe title or the time. The real secret to making  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939800,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the 4-day work week profitable is something \nI call time arbitrage. This is the process  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946440,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of taking the time you bought back at a discount \nand using it to build something you actually own.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 953640,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you take a $20,000 pay cut, but use your 52 \nextra days a year to build a freelance business  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960160,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or a consulting gig, you can often bridge the \nincome gap while maintaining total autonomy.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966520,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because business income allows for tax deductions \nthat W2 income doesn't. You might only need to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 972200,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "earn $15,000 on your own to replace the 20,000 \nyou lost at the office. This is how you diversify  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979640,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your human capital. Relying on one employer for \n100% of your income is a massive risk. Using your  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 987080,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fifth day to build a second uncorrelated income \nstream is like buying insurance for your career.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993880,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even if you only make a few hundred a month, you \nare learning the skills of an entrepreneur. You  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 999560,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are learning how to price your own value, how to \nmarket yourself, and how to manage your own time.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1006160,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Eventually, that side hustle could become \nmore profitable per hour than your day job.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1011920,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At that point, the 4-day work week isn't \na sacrifice at all. It's the launch pad  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1017080,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for your financial independence. You aren't just \nbuying back time. You are buying back your agency.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024880,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We often talk about health as if it is separate \nfrom finance, but they are inextricably linked.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1031400,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chronic stress is one of the most \nexpensive conditions in the modern world.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035720,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It leads to high blood pressure, \nsleep disorders, and burnout.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1039840,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of which carry a heavy price tag in the form \nof medical bills, therapy, and lost productivity.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1046600,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A 3-day weekend provides the biological \nreset that a 2-day weekend simply cannot.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052720,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It allows your nervous system to actually drop \nout of fight or flight mode. People who work 4  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058720,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "days a week report significantly lower levels of \nstress and higher levels of physical activity.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1065360,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That translates to fewer sick days and a longer \nworking life. If you can avoid a stress-induced  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1071800,
    "dDurationMs": 8720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heart attack in your 50s because you reclaimed \nyour Fridays in your 30s, the financial ROI  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1080520,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of that time is infinite. You cannot spend your \nmillions if you are too sick to leave the house.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1085520,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Furthermore, a 3-day weekend gives you \nthe time for preventative maintenance.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1090800,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You have the time to cook nutritious meals, \nexercise consistently, and get 8 hours of sleep.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1097760,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are the foundation of your human \ncapital. If your body is your engine,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1103080,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the 4-day work week is the regular maintenance \nthat prevents a total engine failure.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1108880,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the long run, the healthiest person in the \nroom is often the wealthiest person in the room.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1115120,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most of us are stuck on a hedonic treadmill. \nWe get a raise. We buy a nicer car and within  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1121760,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "6 months that car feels like a baseline. We need \nthe next raise to feel the next hit of dopamine.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1129400,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This lifestyle inflation is why people earning \n$200,000 a year still feel like they are living  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1135400,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paycheck to paycheck. The 4-day work week forces \na radical break from this cycle. By accepting  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1143240,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a 20% pay cut, you are performing a conscious \naudit of your desires. You have to ask yourself,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1150440,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "does this extra spending actually make me happier \nthan an entire extra day of freedom would?  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1157080,
    "dDurationMs": 7080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Usually, the answer is a resounding no. When \nyou work 5 days, you often spend money to treat  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1164160,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yourself for surviving the week. You buy things \nyou don't need to impress people you don't like,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1171000,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all because you are trying to compensate for \nthe fact that you don't own your own time.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1177000,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you own your time, the need for \nthose compensatory purchases vanishes.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1182760,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You find that a walk in the park on a \nFriday morning provides more utility  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1187280,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than a new pair of designer shoes ever could. This \nis the shift from a consumption-based identity  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1193960,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to an autonomy based identity. It is the \nmost powerful financial move you can make  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1199640,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it permanently lowers your cost of \nliving without lowering your quality of life.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1205520,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you are ready to make the jump, do not just \nwalk into your boss's office tomorrow. You need to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1211120,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prove the concept first. I recommend a six-month \nbeta test. Calculate exactly what your new net pay  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1218000,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be, and start living on that amount today. \nTake the difference, that 20% gap, and set up  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1224440,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an automatic transfer to a separate high yield \nsavings account the moment your paycheck hits.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1230880,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you can survive for 6 months without touching \nthat money, you have proven that the 4-day work  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1235780,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "week is financially viable for you. If you \nfind yourself reaching for the credit cards,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1240880,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you have more work to do on your expenses. During \nthis test, you are also building a freedom fund.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1247600,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That 6 months of saved income will act as a buffer \nif your employer decides to prorrate your benefits  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1253600,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or if your side hustle takes longer to start than \nexpected. This is about derisking the transition.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1260320,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You also need to audit your budget categories. \nYour needs, housing and utilities are fixed,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1266400,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so they will take up a larger percentage of \nyour new income. That means your wants must  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1271320,
    "dDurationMs": 7560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be the first thing to go. You are trading the $300 \ndinners for 52 Fridays. Once you have the data and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1278880,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the savings, then you approach the negotiation. \nYou come to the table with a plan, not a plea.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1285600,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You show them how you can be just as productive in \n4 days and you offer a trial period to prove it.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1291680,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You are the one in control. At the end \nof the day, money is just stored energy.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1299400,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is a tool we use to buy things that \nwe hope will make our lives better.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1305280,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we often forget that the most valuable thing \nmoney can buy is your own life back. If you have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1312440,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been running on the treadmill for years and \nyour net worth is growing, but your happiness  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1317080,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is stagnant, it might be time to stop optimizing \nfor the dollar and start optimizing for the hour.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1324960,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want more strategies on how to \nbuild a life of financial autonomy,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1328920,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I invite you to click that join button \nand become one of the optimizers.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1334400,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "members get priority when I'm answering \nquestions and access to a community of people  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1338960,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who are also trying to hack the traditional \neconomic system to find more freedom.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1344640,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whether you decide to take the pay cut \nor not, I want you to remember that you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1348920,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can always earn another dollar, but you cannot \nearn another Tuesday. Take a look at your math,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1356400,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "check your tax brackets, and ask yourself, \nwhat is my fifth day really worth?  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1362880,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'd love to hear your thoughts in the comments. \nWould you take a 20% cut for 50% more free time?  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1370120,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's talk about it. I'm Tom and this is \nTom Talks Money. I'll see you in the next"
    } ]
  } ]
}
